:: HBSC Bank Branch Sneak
<<effects>><<if $avery_fate is "ascended">><<location "avery_skyscraper">><<else>><<location "office">><</if>>
<<set $lock to 1000>>
The bank is closed, but the glass frontage and polished stonework do little to hide the security built into the entrance. <span class="red">Cameras watch the doors from more than one angle.</span>
You move closer anyway, studying the lock and the seams around the frame, wondering whether there is a way in after hours.
<br><br>
<<if currentSkillValue('skulduggery') gte $lock>>
	<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
		You think you could pick the lock, <span class="blue">if your arms weren't bound.</span>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		<<wearProp "lockpick">>
		<span class="green">The lock looks difficult, but not impossible.</span>
		<br><br>
		<<lockicon "pick">><<link [[Try to pick it (0:10)|HBSC Bank Branch Sneak 2]]>><<handheldon>><<pass 10>><<crimeUp 20 "trespassing">><</link>><<crime "trespassing">>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<span class="red">The lock looks far too difficult for you to pick.</span>
	<<skulduggeryrequired>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: HBSC Bank Branch Sneak 2
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist and $xchange.bankHeist.landryReported and crimeSumCurrent() gte 4000>>
	<<generate1>><<person1>>
	You crouch by the bank door and start on the lock. The pick catches, the parts shift, and the latch almost gives.
	<br><br>
	Then the door opens from the inside.
	<br><br>
	A figure in a grey suit looks down at you. Not a guard. Not the police. Someone else. "We've been expecting someone to try this. Come in. We should talk."
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">The bank is on high alert since the break-in.</span>
	<br><<set $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel += 1>>
	<<link [[Go inside|Bank Unrest Interrogation]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	You crouch by the bank door and start on the lock. For a moment, it feels possible. The pick catches, the parts shift, and the latch almost gives.
	<br><br>
	Then a sharp tone chirps above the frame and a metal shutter slams partway down.
	<br><br>
	Two security guards are on you almost at once. One twists your arm behind your back while the other barks into a radio. This branch clearly expects people to try this.
	<span class="red">Your name and face are logged with the police.</span><<crimeUp 1000 "trespassing">><<crime "trespassing">>
	<br>
	<<link [[Next|HBSC Bank Branch Sneak 3]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Bank Unrest Interrogation
<<effects>>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion to 0>>
They lead you through the empty lobby and down a hallway you have never seen before. The lights are dim.
The room at the end has no windows. A single chair is bolted to the floor. The <<person>> in the grey suit closes the door behind you and sits across a small table. Two more suited figures stand behind <<him>>, hands folded.
<br><br>
"Sit."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	You sink into the chair before they have to tell you again. You fold your hands in your lap, but they still tremble slightly.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You sit without hesitation, folding your hands on the table. Something in the room makes it easy to comply.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	You sit carefully and keep your back straight. You hold your expression steady, though it takes more effort than you would like.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	You sit, keeping your expression neutral and your breathing steady.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	You drop into the chair as if it was your idea, trying to look calmer than you feel.
<<else>>
	You sit, keeping your expression neutral.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Let's start with an easy one. What are you doing at this bank, after hours, with a lockpick?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Explain yourself|Bank Unrest Q1]]>><</link>><<englishdifficulty 500 900>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Bank Unrest Q1 Silent]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q1
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "english">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		"I-I lost my card," you stammer. "I thought if I could just get to the ATM inside... I know it was stupid. I'm sorry."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		"I lost my card," you say quietly. "I just wanted to check if it was still inside. I know I should have waited until morning."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		"I misplaced my card this afternoon. I thought it might still be at the counter." You pause. "I realise I should have called ahead instead of coming in person. I apologise."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		"Dare. A friend dared me. Stupid, I know. You got me, fine."
	<<else>>
		"I was trying to retrieve something I left earlier. Bad judgment. I shouldn't have tried to let myself in."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">Your voice stays steady enough</span>. The <<person1>><<person>> watches you, weighing your answer.
<<else>>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		"I... I don't... I'm sorry..." The words don't come. You trail off into silence.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You open your mouth, but only a whisper comes out. "I didn't mean to... I just..."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You start carefully, but your explanation has too many details. The more you say, the worse it sounds.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
		You open your mouth, then close it. Nothing sounds believable. The explanation felt solid in your head, but falls apart as soon as you try to say it.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		"None of your business," you snap. The second the words are out, you know it was a mistake.
	<<else>>
		You open your mouth, then close it. Nothing comes out that sounds believable.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="pink">The <<person1>><<person>> makes a note on a small pad.</span>
	<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 1>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Q2]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q1 Silent
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	You stare at the table. The words won't come, and you don't try to force them.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You fold your hands and sit quietly. There's nothing safe to say.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	You meet <<his>> eyes for a moment, then look away. You say nothing.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	You lean back slightly and say nothing. It's about the only power you have left in here.
<<else>>
	You say nothing. The silence stretches until it feels solid.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> tilts <<his>> head. "Nothing to say? Interesting choice."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 1>>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Q2]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q2
<<effects>>
<<He>> opens a folder. Inside are photographs of you: outside the bank, then inside during your observation visits. Each one has a timestamp.
<br><br>
"You've spent a lot of time here. Then there was an incident. A break-in. Quite a coincidence."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans forward slightly. "We're going to find out who was behind it. We'd prefer to do that quickly. Is there anyone you'd like to tell us about?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Deflect|Bank Unrest Q2 Deflect]]>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty 400 800>>
<br>
<<link [[Give a false name|Bank Unrest Q2 Lie]]>><</link>><<englishdifficulty 600 1000>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse to speak|Bank Unrest Q2 Refuse]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q2 Deflect
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "skulduggery">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		"My account is here," you say carefully. "I come here because that's where my account is. Is that suspicious now?"
		<br><br>
		You add, quietly, "If you have something that actually connects me to what happened, I'd like to know what it is."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		"I bank here," you say. "That's why I visit. That's all there is to it."
		<br><br>
		You pause. "If there's evidence connecting me to something, I'd like to see it."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		"I visit because my account is here. I'm not sure how that becomes evidence of anything." You keep your voice even. "If you have something more specific, I'm happy to answer. Otherwise, I'd appreciate being allowed to go."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		"I bank here. That's it. Mystery solved." You lean forward slightly. "So either show me something real or let me walk."
	<<else>>
		"I come here because my account is here. Are my visits a crime now?" You hold <<his>> gaze. "If you have evidence tying me to whatever happened, show it. Otherwise I'd like to go."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">The <<person1>><<person>> gives nothing away</span>, but the two behind <<him>> exchange a glance.
<<else>>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		You try to sound calm, but your uncertainty shows. You look at the photographs on the table and feel everything start to come apart.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You say the right words, but your voice is too flat and too careful. You do not sound like someone with nothing to hide.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You start well, but your deflection is too rehearsed. The <<person1>><<persons>> expression doesn't change, but something behind <<his>> eyes shifts.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		It comes out too aggressive. Someone with nothing to worry about would not lean forward like that. The <<person1>><<person>> tilts <<his>> head, and you know you misjudged it.
	<<else>>
		You try to sound confident, but your voice gives you away. You look at the photographs and realise how bad they look together.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="pink">The <<person1>><<person>> smiles.</span>
	<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 1>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Q3]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q2 Lie
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 6 "english">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		You give them a name, stumbling through it as if you are reluctant rather than lying. It helps.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You give them a name. Someone distant, barely remembered. You say it plainly, without drama, and that makes it sound real.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You give them a name, with just enough reluctance. You apologise for not mentioning it sooner. The details are believable, vague where they need to be, and uneasy enough to sound real.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		You drop a name as if you are bored of holding it back. The casual tone actually sells it.
	<<else>>
		You give them a name. Someone you know, but not well. Someone who lives far away. The details are believable enough to follow, and vague enough to buy time.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">One of the suited figures steps out to verify.</span>
<<else>>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		You offer a name in a small voice, but the follow-up question is one you can't answer without inventing more. Your hesitation is a different kind that looks like guilt.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You give them a name, but it's too thin. When the follow-up question comes, you have nothing to build on.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You build the lie carefully, but the details do not hold up. One follow-up question exposes a gap, and the next makes it worse.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		You throw out a name, but when they push for details, you have nothing behind it. Bravado does not make a lie hold.
	<<else>>
		You give them a name and a story, but the details are thin. The <<person1>><<person>> asks a follow-up question you can't answer without contradicting yourself.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	"Try again?" <<he>> suggests.
	<br><br>
	<span class="pink">Your lie falls apart.</span>
	<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 2>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Q3]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q2 Refuse
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"I... I don't have anything to say," you murmur.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"I'm afraid I don't have anything useful to tell you," you say.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Not going to happen," you say flatly.
<<else>>
	"I have nothing to say," you say quietly.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> nods slowly. "Noted."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 1>>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Q3]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q3
<<effects>>
<<He>> closes the folder. "One last thing."
<br><br>
<<He>> slides one photograph across the table. At first, you do not recognise the building. Then you do. It is the pub on Harvest Street.
<br><br>
"We've been watching this place. Certain people come and go. People who might know a lot about what happened here." <<He>> taps the photograph. "If you want to tell us anything about them, now would be the time."
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.keptEarpiece>>
	<span class="red">The earpiece in your pocket suddenly feels heavy as lead.</span>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Act ignorant|Bank Unrest Q3 Deny]]>><</link>><<englishdifficulty 700 1200>>
<br>
<<link [[Name Landry|Bank Unrest Q3 Betray]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Bank Unrest Q3 Silent]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
	<span class="blue">Your arms are bound. You can't fight your way out.</span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Rush the door|Bank Unrest Q3 Escape]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty 1 1000>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Bank Unrest Q3 Deny
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 7 "english">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		"I've never been in there," you say, though your voice doesn't quite stay level. "I don't know the people who go there. I can't help you."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		"I've never been inside that pub," you say simply. "I wouldn't know who to name even if I wanted to."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		"I'm afraid I can't help you with that. I don't go to that pub, and I don't know who does."
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		"I don't know that place. Never been in. If you've got a name you want, you'll have to find it yourself."
	<<else>>
		"I've never been inside that pub," you say flatly. "I don't know who drinks there. And I'm not going to invent names to make this go away."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You hold <<his>> gaze</span>. The <<person1>><<person>> doesn't speak for a long moment.
<<else>>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		"I don't... I've never..." You trail off. You can hear how guilty it sounds. You try to recover and only make it worse.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		"I've never—" You stop. Something about the way <<he>> looks at you makes the sentence collapse.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You begin your denial carefully, but then it becomes too careful. Halfway through, you realise it sounds made up rather than remembered.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		"I don't know it, never been—" You stop. Even you can hear it. The denial came too fast.
	<<else>>
		"I don't... I've never..." You trail off. Halfway through, you realise the denial itself gives you away. Normal people do not deny knowledge of a pub they have never visited. They ask questions.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="pink">The <<person1>><<person>> sees it too.</span>
	<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 2>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Verdict]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q3 Escape
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 7 "athletics">>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	Something snaps. You move before you have fully decided, throwing yourself out of the chair towards the door.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	For a moment you consider it. Then you stop thinking and move. You are halfway to the door before anyone reacts.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	Enough of this. You are out of the chair before the thought fully forms, driving hard for the door.
<<else>>
	You lunge out of the chair towards the door. Chairs scrape behind you.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	Your shoulder hits the door at full speed. The latch gives, and you are in the hallway running before they can react.
	<br><br>
	<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "skulduggery">>
	<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
		You remember the layout from your observation visits: service corridor, maintenance hatch, side exit. You are in the alley before they can block the main doors.
		<span class="green">You escaped.</span> But they saw your face, heard your voice, and know exactly who you are.<<crimeUp 500>><<stress 6>><<trauma 6>>
		<br><br>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Next|High Street]]>><<endevent>><<unset $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		You get lost in the corridors. By the time you find an exit, two suited figures are already blocking it.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Caught]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	Hands close on your shoulders before you reach the door. They throw you back into the chair. Hard.<<pain 6>><<gpain>>
	<br><br>
	"Bad decision," the <<person1>><<person>> says.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Caught]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Bank Unrest Q3 Betray
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Landry," you whisper, eyes on the table. "At the pub on Harvest Street. <<nnpc_He "Landry">> planned it."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	"Landry." You say like reading off a name from a list. "The pub on Harvest Street. That's who planned it."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	You take a breath. "The name you want is Landry. <<nnpc_He "Landry">> operates out of a pub on Harvest Street. I believe that's who you're looking for."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Fine. Landry. The Harvest Street pub. That's who you want. Happy now?" you blurt.
<<else>>
	"Landry. At the Harvest Street pub. That's who you're looking for," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> nods slowly. <<He>> closes the folder. "That matches what we already know."<<stress 24>><<trauma 24>>
<br><br>
<span class="pink">You gave them nothing except a betrayal.</span>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 3>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Verdict]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Q3 Silent
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	You look down at the table. You can't bring yourself to say anything.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You keep your hands still and say nothing. The silence answers for you.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	You hold <<his>> gaze and say nothing. There's nothing to say that wouldn't make this worse.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	You cross your arms and say nothing. If they have something on you, let them show it.
<<else>>
	You meet <<his>> eyes and say nothing.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> nods, as if you have confirmed something.
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion += 1>>
<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Verdict]]>><</link>>

:: Bank Unrest Verdict
<<effects>>
<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
<<set _susp to $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion or 0>>
The <<person1>><<person>> sits back and studies you for a long moment.
<br><br>
<<if _al gte 3>>
	/* alertLevel 3: caught no matter what */
	"We appreciate your cooperation," <<he>> says, though <<his>> tone shows no appreciation at all. "Unfortunately, that doesn't change what has to happen next."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> nods to one of the figures behind <<him>>. "Call the police. Have them collect our trespasser. Make sure the charges stick."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Caught]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _susp gte 4>>
	/* High suspicion at any level = arrest */
	"Your story doesn't hold together." <<He>> nods to a colleague. "Call it in."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Bank Unrest Caught]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _al gte 1>>
	/* alertLevel 1-2: pressured release */
	"We'll let you go." <<He>> stands. "But understand this. We know where you live. We know who you speak to. 
	If you come near this building again, or if your name appears in another incident, this conversation will end differently."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> gestures to the door. "Leave. Don't run. Walk out like a customer who took a wrong turn."
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		You keep your eyes down as you're escorted out. Your legs feel unsteady the whole way to the door.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You stand when they tell you to, walk where they direct you, and do not look back. Out is out.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You take a breath and walk out with your head up, keeping your pace steady. It is the only dignity left to take with you.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		You leave without a word. Having the last one would cost more than it is worth right now.
	<<else>>
		You walk out steadily, resisting the urge to move faster than a customer who took a wrong turn.
	<</if>>
	<<stress 18>><<trauma 12>><<gstress>><<gtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><<unset $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion>><</link>>
<<else>>
	/* alertLevel 0: free */
	"We'll let this go," <<he>> says. "The lock-picking is unfortunate, but the damage is minor. Consider this a warning."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> waves to the door. "Go. Don't come back after hours. Use the counter like everyone else."
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
		You nod quickly and leave before anything changes. The cool air outside feels like relief.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You thank them quietly and leave without looking back.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
		You give a brief, calm acknowledgement and show yourself out. There is nothing to gain by staying.
	<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
		You're shown out. You manage not to say anything on the way.
	<<else>>
		You're shown out through the front doors.
	<</if>>
	<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><<unset $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Bank Unrest Caught
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
The <<person1>><<person>> nods to the figures behind <<him>>. Hands clamp down on your shoulders. You're hauled out of the chair.
<br><br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	You don't struggle. You couldn't if you wanted to.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You go where they take you. There's nothing else to do.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	You don't resist. Resistance wouldn't accomplish anything now.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	You think about fighting it. You don't. Two against one in a locked room was never going to end well.
<<else>>
	You let them move you without fighting. The maths does not work in your favour.
<</if>>
<br><br>
They move you to a smaller room and lock the door. Hours pass before the police arrive.<<stress 24>><<trauma 18>><<gggstress>><<gggtrauma>>
<br><br>
<span class="red">You've been arrested.</span><<crimeUp 1000>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Police Prison Intro]]>><<endevent>><<unset $xchange.bankHeist.unrestSuspicion>><<pass 30>><<generatePolice 1>><<generatePolice 2>><</link>>

:: HBSC Bank Branch Sneak 3
<<effects>>
<<if $hbsc.account.level >= 1>>
	<<set _penalty to setup.hbsc.applySneakPenalty()>>
	A manager arrives a moment later, checks your account, and gives you an icy look. "You already bank here? Then listen carefully. You are banned from counter service for <<print _penalty.banDays>> days."
	<<if _penalty.penalty > 0>>
		<br>
		"And because you tried to sneak around inside the branch, we've applied a security penalty of <<printmoney _penalty.penalty>> to your HBSC savings."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	The guards march you back to the pavement and warn you not to try again.
<<else>>
	After a humiliating search and a stern warning, the guards throw you back outside. They tell you the next attempt will go much worse.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<span class="red"><i>This place is too secure for a simple robbery.</i></span>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

/* ================================================================
 * Street event: Master's agents investigating the heist
 * Triggers when heist is reported and crime >= 5000
 * Behaviour scales with $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel
 * ================================================================ */
:: Heist Investigators Widgets [widget]
<<widget "streetHeistInvestigators">>
	<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
	<<if _al lte 0>>
		/* alertLevel 0: Watchers - atmospheric, no danger */
		<<generate1>><<person1>>
		You notice a <<person>> in a dark suit standing very still near a shopfront. <<He>> is not shopping. <<He>> is not waiting for anyone. <<His>> eyes move slowly over the street.
		<<if $awarelevel gte 3>>
			<br><br>
			<span class="red">Something about <<him>> sets you on edge</span>. The stillness. The patience. You have felt this kind of attention before, in the bank and in the vault.
			<<awareness 1>><<gawareness>>
		<<elseif $awarelevel gte 1>>
			<br><br>
			<span class="purple"><<He>> does not look like police</span>. Somehow, that feels worse.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<if $skulduggery gte 600>>
			You spot a second one across the road, acting the same way. <span class="red">They are searching for someone.</span>
			<<if $awarelevel lte 3>>
				<span class="navy">You hope it isn't you.</span>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<br><br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<<elseif _al lte 2>>
		/* alertLevel 1-2: Approach and interrogation */
		<<generate1>><<person1>><<generate2>>
		Two figures in dark suits step out from either side of the pavement, blocking your path. The <<person1>><<person>> is tall and broad-shouldered. <<His>> companion, a <<person2>><<person>>, holds a small leather folder.
		<br><br>
		"Excuse us," the <<person2>><<person>> says. <<His>> voice is polite. Too polite. "We're conducting a private inquiry about the bank. You live in this area, yes?"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Try to slip away|Heist Investigator Flee]]>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>><<athleticsdifficulty 1 800>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Answer their questions|Heist Investigator Questions]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		/* alertLevel 3: Full chase */
		<<generate1>><<person1>><<generate2>>
		You hear tyres screech. A black car pulls up hard against the kerb. Three figures in dark suits get out fast and move straight towards you.
		<br><br>
		The lead figure, a <<person1>><<person>>, points directly at you. "<span class="red">That's the one.</span>"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Run|Heist Investigator Chase 1]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Surrender|Heist Investigator Surrender]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

/* ================================================================
 * Bank event: Security encounter post-heist
 * Different flavor - corporate, cold, procedural
 * ================================================================ */
<<widget "bankHeistSecurityEncounter">>
	<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
	<<generate1>><<person1>>
	<<if _al lte 0>>
		/* Clean heist - subtle unease */
		As you deal with your bank business, you notice a <<person>> in a grey suit watching from behind the glass partition near the service corridor. <<He>> has a clipboard, but <<he>> is not writing anything on it.
		<br><br>
		<<if $awarelevel gte 2>>
			<span class="navy">You recognise the service corridor</span>. You were in there. The memory of the vault and the figure with the antlers comes back.
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>><<trauma 2>><<gtrauma>>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> catches your eye and smiles. The smile does not reach <<his>> eyes.
			<<stress 3>><<gstress>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<<elseif _al lte 2>>
		/* Messy heist - direct questioning */
		You are halfway through your transaction when a <<person>> in a grey suit approaches the counter. <<He>> shows the teller some ID, and the teller immediately steps aside.
		<br><br>
		"A moment of your time," <<he>> says. It is not a question. <<He>> gestures towards a side office. "Routine security review. It won't take long."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Follow quietly|Heist Bank Security Questions]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Refuse and leave|Heist Bank Security Refuse]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<exit>>
	<<else>>
		/* alertLevel 3 - they're waiting for you */
		The moment you step through the door, two guards move to either side of you. A <<person>> in a grey suit steps forward from behind the counter.
		<br><br>
		"We've been expecting someone like you," <<he>> says. "Please come with us. <span class="red">This isn't a request.</span>"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Go quietly|Heist Bank Security Caught]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Break free and run|Heist Bank Security Run]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty 1 1000>><<physiquedifficulty 5000 14000>>
		<br>
		<<exit>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

:: Heist Investigator Flee
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 6 "skulduggery">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	You step sideways, casual as anything, and slip between two parked cars. By the time they react, you are already through a gap in the fence and cutting through a back garden.
	<br><br>
	<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "athletics">>
	<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
		<span class="green">You vault a wall and drop into an alley</span>. Clean escape.
		<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<trauma -6>><<ltrauma>><<crimeUp 300>>
		<br><br>
		<span class="red">But they saw your face</span>. They'll remember it.
		<br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<<else>>
		You scramble over a wall, but your foot catches at the top. You hit the ground hard on the other side.<<pain 4>><<gpain>>
		<br><br>
		You pick yourself up and keep moving. <span class="teal">They do not follow.</span> Maybe watching you run told them enough.
		<<stress -3>><<crimeUp 300>>
		<br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	The <<person1>><<person>> catches your arm before you've taken two steps. <<His>> grip is like iron.
	<br><br>
	"Running makes you look guilty," <<he>> says. "We just want to talk."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Answer their questions|Heist Investigator Questions]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Questions
<<effects>>
<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
The <<person2>><<person>> opens <<his>> leather folder. Inside is a photograph. You can't see it clearly from this angle, but you catch a glimpse of a building. The bank.
<br><br>
"There was an incident at the bank recently," <<he>> says. "A break-in. Careful. Professional." <<He>> watches your face. "You wouldn't know anything about that, would you?"
<br><br>
<<if $english gte 600>>
	<<link [["I heard about it on the news"|Heist Investigator Answer Good]]>><</link>> <span class="green">English</span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<span class="purple"><i>You know you could deflect this better if you had the right words, but they will not come.</i></span>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[I don't know what you're talking about|Heist Investigator Answer Deny]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Heist Investigator Answer Silent]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Heist Investigator Answer Good
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 4 "skulduggery">>
"Terrible business," you say, shaking your head. "I bank there myself. Are my accounts safe?"
<br><br>
The two exchange a glance. The <<person2>><<person>> closes <<his>> folder.
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	"Your accounts are fine," <<he>> says. There's a pause. "Thank you for your time."
	<br><br>
	They step aside and let you pass. <span class="green">You kept calm.</span>
	<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<<else>>
	"Your accounts are fine." <<He>> studies you a moment longer. "We may be in touch."
	<br><br>
	They step aside. <span class="purple">You do not think they fully believed you</span>, but they did not have enough to push further.
	<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Answer Deny
<<effects>>
<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
"I don't know what you're talking about," you say.
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> tilts <<his>> head. "No? Interesting. Because we've been talking to people in this neighbourhood, and your name has come up."
<br><br>
<<if $english gte 400>>
	<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "skulduggery">>
	<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
		"People say all sorts of things," you reply evenly. "Am I being detained?"
		<br><br>
		They exchange another glance. "No," the <<person2>><<person>> says. "Not today."
		<br><br>
		They step aside. <span class="teal">That was close.</span>
		<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<br><br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<<else>>
		"People say all sorts of things," you manage, but your voice wavers.
		<br><br>
		The <<person1>><<person>> smiles. It is not a kind smile. "They do. And some of those things are very specific." <<He>> produces a second photograph. This one shows the east side of the bank and the maintenance hatch.
		<br><br>
		"We'll be watching," <<he>> says. They leave.
		<<stress 12>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<gtrauma>>
		<br><br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if _al gte 2>>
		Your denial sounds flat even to you. The <<person1>><<person>> produces a second photograph. The maintenance hatch on the east wall.
		<br><br>
		"We know someone went through here," <<he>> says. "And we know they had help. Names, faces... we're putting it together."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> leans in. "Last chance. Who planned it?"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Say nothing|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Say I want a lawyer|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		"Hmm." The <<person2>><<person>> makes a note. "We'll be in touch."
		<br><br>
		They leave. <span class="purple">Your hands are shaking.</span>
		<<stress 12>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<gtrauma>>
		<br><br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Answer Silent
<<effects>>
You say nothing. The silence stretches on.
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> studies you. "Silence is an answer too," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
<<if _al gte 2>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> closes <<his>> folder. "We have enough. Come with us."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	They exchange a look, then step aside. "We'll see you again," the <<person2>><<person>> says.
	<<stress 12>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<gtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Arrested
<<effects>>
They take your arms. Not roughly, not gently. Professionally. The black car is still at the kerb, and they guide you into the back seat.
<br><br>
The drive is silent. They do not take you to the police station. They take you somewhere else, to a building with no sign on the door.
<br><br>
After hours of questions you can't answer and threats you can't counter, they hand you over to the police.<<stress 24>><<trauma 18>>
<br><br>
<span class="red">You've been arrested.</span>
<br><<crimeUp 2000>>
<<link [[Next|Police Prison Intro]]>><<endevent>><<pass 30>><<generatePolice 1>><<generatePolice 2>><</link>>

:: Heist Investigator Chase 1
<<effects>>
You bolt. Instinct takes over, and the streets blur around you.
<br><br>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 6 "athletics">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	<span class="green">You're fast.</span> You cut left through a market crowd, weaving between stalls. The shouts behind you start to fade.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Keep running|Heist Investigator Chase 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You sprint hard, but they are faster. One of them is catching up.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Duck into an alley|Heist Investigator Chase Alley]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Try to lose them in the crowd|Heist Investigator Chase Crowd]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Chase 2
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "skulduggery">>
You need to disappear. Running is not enough. They will have more people and more cars.
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	You spot a construction site with scaffolding, tarpaulins, and a gap in the fence. You slide through and press yourself flat behind a skip. Footsteps thunder past.
	<br><br>
	<<bankHeistStealthCheck 4 "science">>
	<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
		You notice the scaffolding connects to a drainage pipe leading down to the storm drains. You could use it to disappear completely.
		<br><br>
		You wait until the footsteps fade, then climb down. By the time they double back, you're underground and gone.<<stress -12>><<trauma -6>><<crimeUp 300>><<llstress>><<lltrauma>>
		<br><br>
		<span class="green">You escaped.</span>
		<br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<<else>>
		You wait behind the skip, heart hammering. Minutes pass. The footsteps don't return.<<stress -6>><<trauma -3>><<crimeUp 300>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">You escaped. Barely.</span>
		<br>
		<<destinationeventend>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You try to squeeze through a gap but your clothes snag. You tear free but the delay costs you.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Climb the scaffolding|Heist Investigator Chase Climb]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty 1 1000>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Hide behind the skip|Heist Investigator Chase Hide]]>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Chase Alley
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 7 "skulduggery">>
You cut hard into a narrow alley. Bins, fire escapes, the smell of grease.
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	You find a recessed doorway and press yourself into it. The pursuers run past the alley entrance without looking.<<stress -6>><<crimeUp 300>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">They missed you.</span>
	<br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<<else>>
	Dead end. A chain-link fence stands ahead, too high to climb quickly. You turn. The <<person1>><<person>> blocks the alley entrance.
	<br><br>
	"Nowhere left to run," <<he>> says.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Chase Crowd
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 6 "skulduggery">>
You push into the densest part of the crowd, hunching low, changing direction twice.
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	You duck into a shop and out through the back door, then through a loading bay, over a wall, and into a residential street.<<stress -9>><<trauma -3>><<crimeUp 300>><<llstress>><<ltrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You lost them.</span>
	<br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<<else>>
	A hand clamps onto your shoulder from behind. "Don't make this harder."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Chase Climb
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 7 "athletics">>
You grab the scaffolding and pull yourself up. Pipes clang beneath your feet.
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	You reach the rooftop and sprint across it. The gap to the next building is narrow. You jump and make it.
	<br><br>
	Below, you hear swearing. They can't follow.<<stress -12>><<trauma -6>><<crimeUp 300>><<llstress>><<lltrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You're free.</span>
	<br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<<else>>
	Your foot slips on a wet bar. You catch yourself, but the delay is enough. A hand grabs your ankle.
	<br><br>
	"Come down. Now."<<pain 8>><<gggpain>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Chase Hide
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 7 "skulduggery">>
You duck behind the skip and press yourself flat against the concrete.
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	Footsteps approach, slow and searching. They check the other side of the skip. A torch beam sweeps above your head.
	<br><br>
	"Not here," someone says. The footsteps move on.
	<br><br>
	You wait a full five minutes before you move. <span class="green">They're gone.</span>
	<<stress -9>><<trauma -6>><<crimeUp 300>>
	<br><br>
	<<destinationeventend>>
<<else>>
	A torch beam finds you immediately. "There."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Investigator Surrender
<<effects>>
You raise your hands. There's no point running from three of them.
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> nods. "Smart."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Investigator Arrested]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Bank Security Questions
<<effects>>
The office is small and has no windows. The <<person>> sits across from you with a folder open. A camera blinks red in the corner.
<br><br>
"This won't take long," <<he>> says. "We're reviewing all clients who visited the branch around the time of the incident. Standard procedure."
<br><br>
<<He>> asks about your account, how often you visit, and why you bank here. Then <<he>> asks the real question.
"Have you ever noticed anything unusual about the service corridors? The maintenance areas?"
<br><br>
<<if $english gte 600>>
	<<link [[I wouldn't know where those are|Heist Bank Security Answer Good]]>><</link>> <span class="green">English</span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<span class="purple"><i>You wish you could sound more convincing, but the right words will not come.</i></span>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[No, nothing|Heist Bank Security Answer Deny]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Heist Bank Security Answer Silent]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Heist Bank Security Answer Good
<<effects>>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 4 "skulduggery">>
"Service corridors?" You frown. "I just use the counter like everyone else. Is there a problem with my account?"
<br><br>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	<<He>> studies you for a long moment, then closes the folder. "No. Your account is in perfect order." <<He>> stands. "Thank you for your cooperation."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> opens the door. <span class="green">You walk out calmly</span>. Nothing to worry about.
	<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<He>> watches you carefully. "Mmhm." <<He>> makes a note. "We'll be reviewing the footage. If anything comes back to you, you know where to find us."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> opens the door. <span class="purple">You're free to go</span>, but you feel eyes on your back all the way out.
	<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Bank Security Answer Deny
<<effects>>
<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
"No," you say. "Nothing unusual."
<br><br>
<<if _al gte 2>>
	<<He>> pulls a photograph from the folder. It shows the maintenance hatch. "This was forced open that night. Whoever did it knew exactly where to find it."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> leans forward. "And our records show you visited this branch seven times in the weeks before the break-in. Different times, every visit. Longer than a normal transaction, every time."
	<br><br>
	<<if $english gte 500>>
		<<link [[I was comparing interest rates|Heist Bank Security Answer Good]]>><</link>> <span class="green">English</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Say nothing more|Heist Bank Security Detained]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<He>> nods and makes a note. "Very well. Thank you for your time."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> opens the door. <span class="purple">The interview felt too easy</span>. Maybe they are waiting for you to make a mistake.
	<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Bank Security Answer Silent
<<effects>>
<<set _al to $xchange.bankHeist.alertLevel or 0>>
You sit in silence. The <<person>> waits. The camera keeps blinking.
<br><br>
<<if _al gte 2>>
	"Silence is noted," <<he>> says. <<He>> presses a button under the desk. The door opens. Two guards enter.
	<br><br>
	"Escort our guest to the holding room. The police will want to speak with <<phim>>."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Heist Bank Security Detained]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	After a very long minute, <<he>> closes the folder. "Thank you for your time." <<His>> tone is cold.
	<br><br>
	You're let out. <span class="pink">That won't be the last time they ask.</span>
	<<stress 12>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<gtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Bank Security Detained
<<effects>>
They move you to a small room deeper in the building. It has no windows. The door locks behind you.
<br><br>
Hours pass. Then the police arrive.<<stress 24>><<trauma 18>><<gggstress>><<gggtrauma>>
<br><br>
<span class="red">You've been arrested.</span>
<br><<crimeUp 2000>>
<<link [[Next|Police Prison Intro]]>><<endevent>><<pass 30>><<generatePolice 1>><<generatePolice 2>><</link>>

:: Heist Bank Security Refuse
<<effects>>
"No, thank you," you say, turning towards the exit. "I'm in a hurry."
<br><br>
The <<person>> doesn't move. "I see." <<He>> nods to the guards.
<br><br>
<<bankHeistStealthCheck 5 "skulduggery">>
<<if _heistStealthResult is "success">>
	You walk quickly but calmly towards the door. The guards hesitate, unsure if they are allowed to physically stop you. 
	By the time they decide, you are through the door and out on the street.
	<br><br>
	<span class="teal">You left before they could press further</span>. But they know your face now.
	<br><<crimeUp 100>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	A guard steps into your path. "The officer asked you to stay," <<he>> says.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Follow to the office|Heist Bank Security Questions]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Push past and run|Heist Bank Security Run]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty 1 1000>>
